          <h3 style="color:white;font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:8px;">🏠 You need to win listings, not just answer them</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin:0;">
            → <strong style="color:white;">B.Claw</strong>, on this one. CMAs built from your MLS comps using NAR PSA methodology, listing descriptions in your brand voice, empty rooms staged into furnished photos and a listing video with voiceover, all from one platform, is a genuinely strong listing-side toolkit at $349 a month on Medium. BirkyStudio has nothing comparable. Our lead side is different: a Verified Prospect List at $497 or $997 one-time is verified, enriched, scored prospects you own, which is about who to call rather than what to show them.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- Final Recommendation -->
      <div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--bs-bg-raised),var(--bs-bg-raised));border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:64px;border:1px solid rgba(255,45,149,0.3);">
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">🏆 The Bottom Line</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          Of every product compared on this site, B.Claw is the one we would recommend without any caveat to a certain kind of agent. It publishes its prices, it gives you a free week with no card, it charges month to month with no lock-in, it connects to the tools you already pay for instead of demanding you replace them, and it does real work: drafts in your voice, CMAs from your comps, listing content, staging, and a briefing on your phone every morning. Its reviews are thin because the real estate product is young, and it says so itself rather than hiding behind a 4.9 average from a different product. If your inbox is the bottleneck, <strong style="color:white;">buy B.Claw and use the free trial before you trust anything on this page, including us</strong>.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          But be equally clear about what it is not. B.Claw is an assistant that makes you faster at work you still have to do. Every reply is a draft you approve, every standing order is something you configured, and when the subscription stops the agent stops. It does not pick up the phone. It does not hold a WhatsApp conversation. It does not supply a single lead. And on the plans an agent actually runs daily it is $2,628 to $4,188 a year, every year, on top of the CRM, the IDX platform and the MLS access you are already paying for, which over three years is about $7,884 to $12,564 for something you will never own. <strong style="color:white;">BirkyStudio is the opposite shape of purchase.</strong> The Base Agent is $1,297 once with the Notion CRM included, the voice and WhatsApp receptionists answer around the clock in two languages for $550 and $297 one-time, the follow-up sends itself without waiting for your approval, and the website and its pages stay yours whether or not we ever speak again.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:24px;">
          The cleanest way to see it: B.Claw is what you buy when you need a faster version of yourself in the inbox. BirkyStudio is what you buy when the phones are ringing and there is nobody to answer them. If both are true, run both, because they do not overlap and the honest answer is that most agents who last do exactly that.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose B.Claw if:</strong> you live in email, you want drafts, CMAs, listing content and staging in one cheap month-to-month agent, and you want to test the whole idea free before you pay.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose BirkyStudio if:</strong> you want your phone and WhatsApp answered 24/7 in two languages, follow-up that sends itself, verified prospects you own, and a one-time price instead of a subscription that never ends.
        </p>
