      <!-- FAQ -->
      <h2 id="faq" style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:16px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div style="margin-bottom:48px;">

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>How much does B.Claw cost?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            B.Claw publishes all of its prices, which is better than most of its competitors. The free plan runs about a week of real use with no credit card, and then Start is $99 a month for roughly 100 actions, Light is $219 a month for roughly 240 actions, Medium is $349 a month for 40 or more actions a day, and Heavy is $599 a month for 80 or more actions a day. Every plan includes every feature, and the only difference is how much the agent runs. Plans are month to month with no annual lock-in and no setup fee, upgrades are prorated, downgrades take effect at the next cycle, and top-ups come in $5 increments inside a comfort zone you set, which defaults to your plan plus $50. Year one on Light is about $2,628, and Medium, the plan described as most popular for agents doing three to five deals a month, is about $4,188.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Does B.Claw answer my phone or reply on WhatsApp?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            No, and this is the single most important thing to understand about it. B.Claw is an AI agent that works inside your Gmail, your calendar and your CRM. It drafts replies for your approval, pulls MLS comps for a CMA, writes listing content, stages listing photos, runs a morning briefing and keeps a memory of every promise you made. What it does not do is pick up a phone call or hold a WhatsApp conversation, and Bounti does not claim otherwise. Its own pricing page says every plan gets the whole agent: briefings, triage, CMAs, listing prep, memory and standing orders. Answering calls and messages is a different product, and that product is BirkyStudio's: the Voice Receptionist is $550 one-time plus Vapi usage of about $30 to $50 a month and answers calls 24/7 in English and Spanish, and the WhatsApp Text Receptionist is $297 one-time.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>How is B.Claw different from BirkyStudio's The Base Agent?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            They are both an AI layer that works across your tools, which is why this page pairs them. The difference is who does the work and when it stops. B.Claw is a subscription you operate: it drafts, you approve, you send, and the bill continues for as long as you want it. It runs from $99 to $599 a month forever, so $1,188 to $7,188 a year, every year. The Base Agent is a build we do for you one time for $1,297, with the Notion CRM included free, and after that the only optional cost is care at $97 a month. On the plans an agent actually runs daily, Light at $2,628 a year and Medium at $4,188 a year each cost more in year one than The Base Agent plus a year of care at about $2,461, and unlike a one-time build the subscription never ends.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Is B.Claw (Bounti) the same as OpenClaw or other Claw tools?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            No, and the names do get mixed up. B.Claw is the name of the AI agent sold by Bounti, a company whose product is built specifically around the real estate agent workflow: Gmail, Google Calendar, MLS comps, CMAs, listings and 250 or more connected tools. OpenClaw is an unrelated open-source project that runs on a server you host and maintain yourself, which is why the agents discussing it in forums talk about VPS and AWS upkeep and about rebuilding integrations that established automation platforms already provide. So when you read a forum thread about Claw, check which product is actually being discussed before you take the opinion as a review of Bounti. The two are not the same purchase and the support experience is not comparable either, because one is a hosted product with a vendor behind it and the other is software you run.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Does B.Claw have a contract, a setup fee or a free trial?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            This is where B.Claw is genuinely clean, and it is worth saying clearly. There is a free trial of about a week with no credit card and every feature included, there is no setup fee, every plan is month to month with no annual lock-in, upgrades are prorated, and there is no cancellation penalty. Its own pricing page states there are no annual or volume discounts because pricing is the same month to month for everyone, with no negotiated rates. That is a fairer buying experience than BoldTrail, CINC or Sierra Interactive, all of which hide the price or lock you into twelve months. BirkyStudio is also contract free with no minimum term and a 30 day money back guarantee on the build, and the pattern across both products is that the cheapest thing to compare is not the monthly number but the exit.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Does B.Claw include an IDX website or lead generation?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            No. B.Claw rides on the real estate stack you already pay for rather than replacing it, and its own comparison page is explicit that it has no IDX website, describing it as riding on your existing IDX. It also does not supply leads. What it does is work the leads and the listings you already have: it drafts every reply for approval, triggers instant response on a new lead, prepares CMAs from your MLS comps, and updates a pipeline sheet from your inbox. If you need an IDX site, that comes from a platform such as BoldTrail, Sierra Interactive or Placester, or from your MLS website vendor. BirkyStudio is in a third category again: we build general business websites at $499, $999 and $1,999 one-time, and our Verified Prospect List at $497 or $997 one-time is a file of verified, enriched, scored prospects you own, not an IDX feed.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Is B.Claw a good fit for a team or a brokerage?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            Not today, and Bounti says so itself. Its pricing FAQ answers the team question directly: not yet, B.Claw is a single-agent product today, each agent runs their own subscription with their own Gmail, calendar and CRM connections, and multi-agent, shared inbox and brokerage tiers are on the roadmap but not shipping. So a five person team is five subscriptions at $99 to $599 each per month, which is $5,940 to $35,940 a year, with no shared inbox and no brokerage roll-up. BirkyStudio's business tier starts at $2,997 one-time for The Base Agent and does not multiply by seat. For a brokerage that wants one system for IDX, lead routing, commissions and recruiting, neither of these is the answer and a platform such as BoldTrail is.
          </div>
        </details>

      </div>

